    "rawResponses": {
      "classes": "1: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes a bank.\n2: NO MATCH -- An IT operations team is only one type of organizational unit.\n3: MATCH 2 -- Both denote the IT operations team.\n4: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes a service desk.\n5: NO MATCH -- An IT operations team is not specifically a network operations centre.\n6: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes a security operations centre.\n7: NO MATCH -- An IT operations team is not an incident response team.\n8: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes an incident commander.\n9: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes an application owner.\n10: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes a technical owner.\n11: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes a business owner.\n12: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes a vendor.\n13: MATCH 6 -- Both denote a regulatory authority.\n14: NO MATCH -- An IT service is not a business process.\n15: MATCH 1 -- Both denote an IT service.\n16: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes a service level objective.\n17: NO MATCH -- An IT service is not an application.\n18: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes a database.\n19: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes an infrastructure component.\n20: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes a server.\n21: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes a virtual machine.\n22: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes a container platform.\n23: NO MATCH -- An IT service is not specifically a cloud service.\n24: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes a network device.\n25: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes a network segment.\n26: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes an endpoint.\n27: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes a storage system.\n28: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes a data centre.\n29: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes a site.\n30: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes an environment.\n31: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes a data asset.\n32: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes an integration interface.\n33: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes a monitoring tool.\n34: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes a monitoring rule.\n35: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes a metric.\n36: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes a log source.\n37: NO MATCH -- A containment measure is an action, not a security event.\n38: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes a major incident.\n39: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes a cybersecurity incident.\n40: MATCH 3 -- Both denote a diagnosed, known problem.\n41: NO MATCH -- A containment measure is not an emergency change.\n42: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes a release.\n43: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes a business continuity plan.\n44: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes a disaster recovery test.\n45: MATCH 4 -- Both denote incident-related communication to an audience.",
      "relationships": "1: MATCH 3 -- A resolver group having an on-call engineer expresses the engineer’s membership.\n2: NO MATCH -- No candidate links a stakeholder’s interest to a business service.\n3: NO MATCH -- No candidate describes delivery through a customer channel.\n4: NO MATCH -- No candidate links a backup set to a configuration item.\n5: NO MATCH -- No candidate links a recovery plan to a backup set.\n6: NO MATCH -- No candidate links an event to a configuration item.\n7: NO MATCH -- No candidate describes an alert indicating an event.\n8: NO MATCH -- No candidate links an alert to a configuration item.\n9: NO MATCH -- Correlation with an alert is not an alert opening an incident.\n10: MATCH 7 -- Both describe the incident’s correlation with an event.\n11: MATCH 2 -- Impacting a configuration item means affecting it.\n12: NO MATCH -- Assignment to an engineer is not the same as being handled by one.\n13: NO MATCH -- No candidate links an incident to a runbook.\n14: MATCH 9 -- An incident having evidence expresses its support by evidence items.\n15: NO MATCH -- No candidate describes an incident notifying a stakeholder.\n16: NO MATCH -- No candidate describes a change resolving an incident.\n17: NO MATCH -- No candidate links an incident to a recovery plan.\n18: NO MATCH -- No candidate links an incident to a materiality assessment.\n19: NO MATCH -- No candidate links an incident to a post-incident review.\n20: NO MATCH -- No candidate links a workaround to a runbook.\n21: NO MATCH -- Deployment implementing a change is not change modifying a configuration item.\n22: NO MATCH -- No candidate describes a review identifying a problem.\n23: NO MATCH -- No candidate describes a review producing a corrective action.\n24: NO MATCH -- No candidate links a corrective action to a change.\n25: NO MATCH -- No candidate links a materiality assessment to a regulatory notification.\n26: NO MATCH -- No candidate describes a regulatory notification reporting an incident.\n27: NO MATCH -- No candidate links a regulatory notification to an evidence item."
